        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0a4e962e-834a-5bf5-a176-c347a554d06b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Svalbard, Jan Mayen, Norway\n- Systems: ISO 3166-1, ISO 3166-1 numeric, UN M.49\n- Organizations: United Nations Statistics Division\n\nFacts:\n- Svalbard and Jan Mayen is an ISO 3166-1 statistical designation for two parts of Norway under separate jurisdictions: Svalbard and Jan Mayen.\n- ISO 3166-1 assigns Svalbard and Jan Mayen the alpha-2 code SJ, the alpha-3 code SJM, and the numeric code 744.\n- ISO 3166-1 numeric codes are similar to the three-digit country codes developed and maintained by the United Nations Statistics Division.\n- ISO 3166-1 numeric codes originate from the United Nations Statistics Division standard UN M.49.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6ab1ee8b-f637-5956-b359-0a9541293bda",
        "text": "Page: Svalbard and Jan Mayen. Sentence: Svalbard and Jan Mayen (Norwegian: \"Svalbard og Jan Mayen\" , ISO 3166-1 alpha-2: SJ, ISO 3166-1 alpha-3: SJM, ISO 3166-1 numeric: 744) is a statistical designation defined by ISO 3166-1 of two parts of Norway under separate jurisdictions—Svalbard and Jan Mayen.\nPage: ISO 3166-1 numeric. Sentence: They are similar to the three-digit country codes developed and maintained by the United Nations Statistics Division, from which they originate in its UN M.49 standard.",
